  "derivation": [
    "The real square root is nonnegative, so sqrt(x^2)=|x| for every real x.",
    "For x<0, |x|=-x. For x>0, |x|=x. At x=0, |x|=0.",
    "The original denominator excludes zero in tasks a and b; algebraic cancellation does not restore that input.",
    "Tasks c and d have no denominator or additional square-root restriction, so their domain is all real numbers."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "962-a",
      "source_task_label": "\u0430",
      "formula": "y=sqrt(x^2)/x",
      "domain": "(-infinity,0) union (0,infinity)",
      "range": ["-1", "1"],
      "branches": [
        {"condition": "x<0", "formula": "y=-1", "shape": "left horizontal ray"},
        {"condition": "x>0", "formula": "y=1", "shape": "right horizontal ray"}
      ],
      "reasoning": "For x<0, (-x)/x=-1; for x>0, x/x=1. These simplifications apply only where x is nonzero.",
      "zero": {
        "defined": false,
        "value": null,
        "included_points": [],
        "open_endpoints": [["0", "-1"], ["0", "1"]],
        "left_limit": "-1",
        "right_limit": "1",
        "classification": "jump with two excluded ray endpoints, not one removable hole",
        "origin_on_graph": false
      },
      "half_parabolas": [],
